#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Auracular - AUR Heuristic Threat Model.

Not a verdict - a heuristic ranking to tell you which AUR packages deserve a
manual look before (or after) install. High score = fewer red flags, not
"proven safe". Anything flagged should still be read by a human.

Checks each package's AUR metadata, its PKGBUILD text, and its git commit
history (for a dormant-package-quietly-taken-over pattern) - not proof of
safety or malice, just signals worth attention.

Usage:
    auracular                        # no args = score every installed AUR package
    auracular pkgname [pkgname2 ...] # check specific package(s) instead, e.g. before installing
    auracular -v                     # also show matched PKGBUILD lines
    auracular --no-history           # skip the git-clone handoff check (faster)
    auracular --explain pkgname      # plain-English, annotated PKGBUILD walkthrough
"""
